            "text": "{\"claims\":[{\"type\":\"extra_hyp\",\"location\":\"Differentiable ℝ f ∧ (Differentiable ℝ (deriv f))\",\"explanation\":\"The informal bounds concern an interval, but this hypothesis requires f and its derivative to be differentiable on all of ℝ. A function can be twice differentiable throughout the interval while failing to be differentiable elsewhere.\",\"prediction\":\"The edited interval-local hypothesis admits some functions excluded by the original global hypothesis.\",\"probe_kind\":\"hypothesis_separation\",\"comparison\":null,\"witnesses\":null,\"edit_from\":\"Differentiable ℝ f ∧ (Differentiable ℝ (deriv f))\",\"edit_to\":\"∀ x ∈ Set.Icc a b, DifferentiableAt ℝ f x ∧ DifferentiableAt ℝ (deriv f) x\",\"bridge\":\"translated\",\"obligation\":\"Check whether the informal problem implicitly intends global twice differentiability; the separation test alone does not settle that interpretation.\"}],\"summary\":\"One testable suspicion: the Lean hypothesis may impose differentiability outside the interval unnecessarily.\"}"
